#comment A REAL redraw witness, small enough to check by hand.
#comment
#comment E is the 4-vertex lattice curve below. Down z (the xy view) its first
#comment and third edges cross at (1,1), separated in z, so project(E) is the
#comment single-crossing curl carried here. Rotating by x->y->z->x carries the
#comment crossing out of view, so project(R*E) is a crossingless circle: the
#comment component comes free, is named by '#spinoffs colors=0', and the next
#comment record carries no diagram (a 0-crossing summand).
#comment
#comment The snapshot is v1 internal state, NOT a PD row, deliberately: a
#comment one-crossing curl is the one diagram whose PD row is ambiguous -- the
#comment row `1 0 0 1 -1` that knoodlesimplify writes for this curve reads back
#comment with the OPPOSITE handedness, which the colour-kept isomorphism of
#comment check 1 (correctly) refuses. Internal state is label-exact.
#comment The stream is v0 anyway, because v1 makes '#state' mandatory and so has
#comment no spelling for the empty record that ends this trace.
#comment
#comment Generated 2026-09-23 by projecting E with LinkEmbedding4<Int64> (the
#comment projector knoodleprove trusts). Do not hand-edit the #state block.
